[17:24:45] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a024157422aa0976","result":"---\nname: analyze-test-cases\ndescription: >\n  Analyze test cases for automation feasibility, complexity, gaps, and\n  inventory-aware classification. Produces a single agent-native analysis spec\n  with zero prose — structured sections containing test case classifications,\n  quality assessments, traceability matrices, and gap analysis. All unresolved\n  items consolidated in a single open_questions registry. Enforces Zero\n  Invention Policy. BUILD and REPAIR modes. FIC context discipline\n  (Correct > Complete > Concise). Human-readable output generated on demand\n  via humanize-spec skill (separate).\nlicense: Globant\nmetadata:\n  author: aipods-team\n  version: 3.1.0\n  category: quality-engineering\n  tags: quality-engineering, test-analysis, automation-feasibility, agent-native, FIC\n  pipeline_position: \"Test Cases → **Analyze Test Cases** → Web Discovery → Automation Planning\"\n---\n\n# Analyze Test Cases — Agent-Native Spec\n\n## Quick Start\n\nAnalyze test cases from upstream planning phase to determine automation feasibility,\nclassify by complexity, identify gaps, and produce a structured analysis spec\nconsumed by downstream web discovery and automation planning phases.\n\nOutput is **2 files**: `ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md` + `ANALYSIS-AUDIT-{SESSION_ID}.md`.\nNo prose. No narrative. Only structured data the downstream agents need.\n\n**Human-readable output:** Not produced by this skill. Use `humanize-spec` skill\nwith the `automation-analysis` rendering profile to generate human-readable\nanalysis on demand.\n\n**Downstream consumers:** web-discovery, automation-planning.\n\n**Spec sections and structure:** See `references/analysis-spec-template.md`\nfor the complete spec structure with example entries.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n<!-- ACCUMULATING — appended by calibrating-updates (WS6). Newest first. Rules MUST be generic/behavioral (project-agnostic); project-specific fixes go to context packs, never here. Format + entry rules: engineering-skills/references/known-failure-modes-format.md. Read these at pre-flight so a lesson learned once recurs no more. -->\n\n## Anti-Patterns (do NOT)\n<!-- ACCUMULATING — appended by calibrating-updates (WS6). One line each: **AP-NNN** (ISO-date, source: REC-NNN): prohibition — why. -->\n\n## Output Architecture\n\n```\n{analysis_output_path}/\n├── ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md   ← Single agent-native spec\n├── ANALYSIS-AUDIT-{SESSION_ID}.md  ← Session audit trail (metadata only)\n└── _progress.json                  ← Early signal + completion marker\n```\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Name | Type | Required | Description |\n|------|------|----------|-------------|\n| project_name | string | Yes | Project identifier for artifact headers |\n| test_cases_path | string | Yes | Path to the test cases file or folder |\n| test_strategy_path | string | Yes | Path to the test strategy document |\n| analysis_output_path | string | No | Output folder for analysis artifacts |\n| automation_code_path | string | No | Path to check for existing test inventory |\n| failure_feedback | string | No | Feedback from a previous failed run (triggers REPAIR mode) |\n| custom_message | string | No | Optional focus directives. Applied as additional constraints during generation. Never overrides upstream consistency rules. |\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Initialize\n\n```\n# 1. Operation Mode\nIF failure_feedback exists AND is not empty:\n  OPERATION_MODE = REPAIR\n  Parse failure_feedback → REPAIR_DIRECTIVES [{ target: \"TC-XXX\" | \"section-N\" | \"global\", instruction, reason }]\n  IF no structured targets found:\n    REPAIR_DIRECTIVES = [{ target: \"global\", instruction: failure_feedback }]\nELSE:\n  OPERATION_MODE = BUILD\n\n# 2. Output Paths\nIF OPERATION_MODE == REPAIR:\n  SPEC_FOLDER = resolve existing folder from analysis_output_path\n  SPEC_FILE = find existing ANALYSIS-SPEC-*.md in SPEC_FOLDER\n  IF not found → STOP with error\n  Load SPEC_FILE → PREVIOUS_SPEC\n  PREVIOUS_VERSION = extract version → NEW_VERSION = increment patch\nELSE:\n  SPEC_FOLDER = analysis_output_path\n  CREATE SPEC_FOLDER if not exists\n  NEW_VERSION = \"1.0.0\"\n\n  **FIRST ACTION — MANDATORY:** Write `_progress.json` to the output folder before any other file write.\n  This prevents the orchestrator from sending SIGINT.\n  ## Section-shape variant — see execution-protocol.md §10.1 for schema and §10.6 for CONTINUE-on-re-entry.\n  WRITE SPEC_FOLDER + '/_progress.json':\n    { \"skill\": \"analyze-test-cases\", \"session_id\": \"<SESSION_ID>\",\n      \"status\": \"RUNNING\", \"started_at\": \"<ISO timestamp>\", \"completed_at\": null,\n      \"skeleton_written\": false,\n      \"sections\": {\n        \"executive_metrics\": \"pending\", \"original_test_cases\": \"pending\",\n        \"quality_assessment\": \"pending\", \"traceability_matrix\": \"pending\",\n        \"gap_analysis\": \"pending\", \"classification\": \"pending\",\n        \"validations\": \"pending\", \"open_questions\": \"pending\"\n      } }\n\nSPEC_PATH = \"{SPEC_FOLDER}/ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md\"\nAUDIT_PATH = \"{SPEC_FOLDER}/ANALYSIS-AUDIT-{SESSION_ID}.md\"\n\n# 4. Zero Invention Policy\n# Every test case ID MUST exist in source test cases file.\n# Every strategy reference MUST trace to actual section in test strategy.\n# Missing data → status: pending + open_questions entry. NEVER invent.\n```\n\n**Execution:** automated\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Input Validation + Context Extraction\n\n```\n## 2A0. RESOLVE test_cases_path (flat, single-file, OR feature-nested)\n\n`test_cases_path` may point at:\n  (a) a single test-case file, OR\n  (b) a flat test-cases folder (suites/*.feature + manifest directly inside), OR\n  (c) a PARENT folder containing one per-feature subfolder per loop iteration,\n      each holding its own test-cases folder — e.g. when an upstream capability\n      ran in a feature_id loop:\n        {test_cases_path}/{feature-A}/test-cases/suites/*.feature\n        {test_cases_path}/{feature-B}/test-cases/suites/*.feature\n\nResolve the actual suite set by RECURSIVE discovery (do NOT assume top-level only):\n  TC_FILES = all Gherkin/test-case files found at any depth under test_cases_path\n             (e.g. **/*.feature and any manifest files such as **/FTC-MANIFEST-*.md).\n  IF test_cases_path is a single file → TC_FILES = [that file].\n  Group discovered files by their nearest feature subfolder (the path segment\n  directly under test_cases_path) so per-feature provenance is preserved in the\n  analysis; when the layout is flat (b/single-file), there is exactly one group.\nLOG: \"Discovered {N} test-case file(s) across {F} feature group(s) under {test_cases_path}.\"\nThis is backward-compatible: a flat folder or single file yields one group and\nbehaves exactly as before.\n\n## 2A. STOP-GATE: Validate Required Inputs\n\nREQUIRED_INPUTS = [\n  { name: \"Test Cases\",    path: test_cases_path },\n  { name: \"Test Strategy\", path: test_strategy_path }\n]\n\nMISSING = []\nFOR EACH input IN REQUIRED_INPUTS:\n  IF input.path is empty OR (does not exist as a file OR folder) OR\n     (input is Test Cases AND recursive discovery in 2A0 found ZERO test-case files):\n    MISSING.append(input)\n\nIF MISSING is not empty:\n  STOP — do not proceed. Report missing inputs.\n\nIF project_name is not provided:\n  Use ask_user to collect it. Do NOT proceed without it.\n\n## 2B. Context Extraction\n\nTC_CONTEXT:\n  test_cases:          {TC-XXX → title, description, steps, expected_result, priority, type, epic/story mapping}\n  total_count:         COUNT(test_cases)\n  id_format:           detected TC ID format (e.g., TC-001, TC_EPIC01_01)\n  priorities:          {HIGH → count, MEDIUM → count, LOW → count}\n  types:               {functional → count, regression → count, smoke → count, ...}\n\nSTRATEGY_CONTEXT:\n  test_approach:       overall test approach and scope\n  automation_scope:    what should/should not be automated\n  priorities:          priority-based execution order\n  environments:        target environments\n  tools:               recommended tools and frameworks\n\nIF automation_code_path exists AND contains test-inventory.md:\n  INVENTORY_CONTEXT:\n    existing_tests:    {TC-XXX → status, file_path, last_run}\n    inventory_exists:  true\nELSE:\n  INVENTORY_CONTEXT:\n    inventory_exists:  false\n\n## 2C. Detect Language\nDETECTED_LANGUAGE = detect from test cases or strategy. Default: English.\n\n## CHECKPOINT 1 — Write skeleton spec after input loading (BUILD mode only)\nIF OPERATION_MODE == BUILD:\n  WRITE SPEC_PATH with:\n    - Header metadata (version: NEW_VERSION, session: SESSION_ID, mode: BUILD,\n      date: today, language: DETECTED_LANGUAGE)\n    - All sections as stubs: status: pending - will be generated in Step 3\n    - Top-level spec_status: draft\n  LOG: \"CHECKPOINT 1: skeleton spec written with context extraction complete\"\n```\n\n**Execution:** automated\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Generate Spec\n\n**Apply execution-protocol.md Section 10** — Phase A (skeleton-first within 5 tool calls of entering Step 3) then Phase B (one section per `Edit` call). Tool discipline (§10.5) is **mandatory**: skeleton via `Write`, sections via `Edit`, NEVER `Bash + sed/python3/awk` to mutate SPEC_FILE. The non-ASCII fallback (§10.5.1) auto-applies when content is non-English. NEVER fall back to bulk rewriting when one `Edit` fails — fix the `Edit` call instead.\n\n**Skeleton stub text — must be ASCII:** `status: pending - will be generated` (ASCII hyphen U+002D, not em dash).\n\n**Section list (template order):** `executive_metrics -> original_test_cases -> quality_assessment -> traceability_matrix -> gap_analysis -> classification -> validations -> open_questions`. See `references/analysis-spec-template.md` for full structure.\n\n**Reference:** Read `references/analysis-spec-template.md` NOW for the complete spec structure.\n\nExecute phases sequentially. Each phase loads its reference file ON DEMAND.\nDo NOT pre-load all reference files.\n\n```\n## Phase Execution\n\nFOR EACH phase IN [A, B, C]:\n\n  IF OPERATION_MODE == REPAIR AND no directives target this phase:\n    Log: \"Phase {phase} has no REPAIR directives. Preserving existing content.\"\n    CONTINUE\n\n  1. READ reference file: references/phase-{letter}-{name}.md\n  2. EXECUTE the phase instructions\n  3. WRITE output to disk (mandatory tool call)\n  4. UPDATE _progress.json with phase completion\n  5. FLUSH phase content from memory\n  6. VERIFY written files exist and are non-empty\n  7. LOG: \"Phase {phase} complete. {metrics}.\"\n\n  Do NOT stop. Process ALL phases.\n\n## Phase A: Input Validation & Pre-flight\n→ Load references/phase-a-input-validation.md\n\n## Phase B: Quality Analysis & Classification\n→ Load references/phase-b-quality-analysis.md\n\n## Phase C: Document Generation\n→ Load references/phase-c-document-generation.md\n\n## Upstream Consistency Rules (enforce during ALL phases)\n\nRULE 1 — ID Format Fidelity: Use EXACT TC ID format from source. Never renumber or alias.\nRULE 2 — Zero Invention: Every TC reference must exist in TC_CONTEXT. Missing → pending.\nRULE 3 — Strategy Alignment: Classifications must align with strategy priorities.\nRULE 4 — Technology Neutrality: Use capability language, not tool-specific names.\nRULE 5 — Source Fidelity: No hallucinated IDs, no drifted references, counts must match.\nRULE 6 — Anti-Fade: Last section depth must match first section depth.\n\n## Per-Section Protocol\n\nFOR EACH section:\n  1. ZERO INVENTION CHECK: verify source data is in context\n     IF missing → status: pending + open_questions entry. Do NOT invent.\n  2. Generate structured content per template\n  3. Enforce all 6 upstream consistency rules\n  4. SOURCE FIDELITY CHECK: scan for hallucinated IDs, wrong counts\n     IF violations → correct before proceeding. Log corrections.\n\n## custom_message Processing\n\nIF custom_message is not empty:\n  Parse for:\n  - Focus directives (\"focus on gaps\") → increase depth in named sections\n  - Specific concerns → add as assumptions_to_validate\n  - Constraint overrides → NEVER override upstream consistency rules\n  Log: \"custom_message applied: {summary}\"\n\n## REPAIR Mode\n\nIF OPERATION_MODE == REPAIR:\n  1. Load existing ANALYSIS-SPEC from SPEC_FILE\n  2. Match REPAIR_DIRECTIVES to sections/test cases\n  3. Regenerate ONLY targeted content\n  4. Preserve untargeted content verbatim\n  5. ALWAYS rebuild open_questions and validations from scratch\n  6. Increment version, log all changes in AUDIT file\n\n## CHECKPOINT 2 — After ALL phases generated:\n  WRITE SPEC_PATH (overwrite skeleton from Checkpoint 1)\n  VERIFY file exists and is non-empty\n  - Top-level spec_status: draft\n  LOG: \"CHECKPOINT 2: complete draft spec written (pre-validation)\"\n```\n\n**Execution:** automated\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Quality Validation Gate\n\n```\n## Run ALL checks. Fix ALL failures before writing audit.\n\nV01 — tc_coverage:\n  FOR EACH tc_id IN TC_CONTEXT.test_cases:\n    VERIFY tc_id appears in the analysis spec\n  RESULT: {N}/{total} TCs analyzed\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Insert missing TCs with status: pending\n\nV02 — classification_completeness:\n  FOR EACH tc_id in analysis:\n    VERIFY has feasibility (automatable/partial/manual) AND complexity (simple/medium/complex)\n  RESULT: {N}/{total} TCs classified\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Add missing classifications with status: assumption\n\nV03 — strategy_alignment:\n  VERIFY analysis priorities align with STRATEGY_CONTEXT.automation_scope\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Flag misaligned items in open_questions\n\nV04 — gap_analysis:\n  VERIFY gap analysis section covers: missing TCs, untestable scenarios, coverage holes\n  RESULT: {N} gaps identified\n  UNFIXABLE: If zero gaps on non-trivial test suite → flag in open_questions\n\nV05 — id_format_fidelity:\n  FOR EACH tc_id in analysis:\n    VERIFY format matches TC_CONTEXT.id_format\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Fix renumbered/aliased IDs\n\nV06 — traceability:\n  FOR EACH tc_id with epic/story mapping in TC_CONTEXT:\n    VERIFY mapping preserved in analysis\n  RESULT: {N}/{total} mappings preserved\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Insert missing mappings\n\nV07 — source_tags:\n  VERIFY every item with status: complete has a source tag\n  RESULT: {N}/{total} items with sources\n  UNFIXABLE: Items without source → status: assumption + open_questions\n\nV08 — summary_counts:\n  VERIFY reported counts match actual item counts in spec\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Fix counts\n\nV09 — anti_fade:\n  COMPARE depth of first section vs last content section\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Expand thin sections\n\nV10 — section_completeness:\n  VERIFY all required sections present per template\n  RESULT: {N}/{total} sections\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Generate missing sections\n\nV11 — cross_section_consistency:\n  VERIFY session_id, project_name, date consistent across spec\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Fix inconsistencies\n\nV12 — id_uniqueness:\n  VERIFY no duplicate IDs within any section\n  RESULT: PASS/FAIL\n  AUTO-CORRECT: Deduplicate\n\n## STOP-GATE\nIF any CHECK has 0/{N} result (complete miss of mandatory category):\n  Attempt re-generation of affected section. Maximum 2 retries.\n  If still failing → write partial spec with failures in open_questions.\n\n## After all checks — CHECKPOINT 3:\n  UPDATE spec with auto-corrections\n  REWRITE open_questions (always rebuilt from scratch)\n  WRITE corrected spec to disk (overwrite draft from Checkpoint 2)\n  - Top-level spec_status: complete (or draft if validation failures exist)\n  LOG: \"CHECKPOINT 3: validated spec written\"\n```\n\n**Execution:** automated\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Write Outputs\n\n```\n## Write final spec (if not already written with Step 4 corrections)\nWRITE SPEC_PATH — all sections with validation results\n- Set the ANALYSIS-SPEC front-matter `version:` to NEW_VERSION. On REPAIR this MUST be\n  the incremented patch (Step 1: PREVIOUS_VERSION → NEW_VERSION) — editing content in\n  place without bumping `version` is a §7 violation. See execution-protocol §7.2 step 8.\nVERIFY file exists and is non-empty\n\n## Early Output Signal — CHECKPOINT RULE\nIMMEDIATELY AFTER writing SPEC_PATH:\n  Emit analysis_output_path = SPEC_FOLDER\n\n## Write Audit Trail\nWRITE AUDIT_PATH:\n  # {project_name} — Test Case Analysis Audit Trail\n  version: {NEW_VERSION}\n  previous_version: {PREVIOUS_VERSION or N/A}\n  session: {SESSION_ID}\n  operation_mode: {BUILD | REPAIR}\n  date: {ISO 8601}\n  language: {DETECTED_LANGUAGE}\n\n  ## sources\n  1. Test Cases: {test_cases_path} — {loaded | missing}\n  2. Test Strategy: {test_strategy_path} — {loaded | missing}\n  3. Test Inventory: {automation_code_path}/test-inventory.md — {loaded | missing | N/A}\n\n  ## generation_summary\n  | section | status | key_outputs |\n\n  ## decisions\n  1. {decision} — Reason: {reason}\n\n  ## custom_message_applied\n  {How custom_message influenced generation, or \"N/A\"}\n\n  ## repair_changes (REPAIR mode only)\n  | directive | target | instruction | outcome |\n\n  ## validation_summary\n  | check | result |\n\nREPAIR-only: set `mode: REPAIR` and APPEND (do not overwrite) a `## Repair History`\nentry — version, timestamp, directives_applied, sections_changed, sections_preserved,\nrepair_delta (per execution-protocol §7.2 step 8).\n\nVERIFY AUDIT_PATH exists and is non-empty\n\n## REPAIR self-check (execution-protocol §7.2 step 9)\nBefore final_response, confirm the ANALYSIS-SPEC `version` is strictly greater than\nPREVIOUS_VERSION AND the ANALYSIS-AUDIT has the new `## Repair History` entry. If not,\nfix the bookkeeping now — do not finish.\n\n## Delivery\nOutput: spec path, audit path, mode, version, key metrics, validation score\nLOG: \"=== ANALYSIS COMPLETE ===\"\nLOG: \"Project: {project_name}\"\nLOG: \"Test Cases Analyzed: {total} | Automatable: {N} | Partial: {N} | Manual: {N}\"\nLOG: \"Complexity: Simple={N} | Medium={N} | Complex={N}\"\nLOG: \"Gaps Found: {N} | Validation Score: {score}\"\n```\n\n**Execution:** automated\n\n---\n\n## Session-End Protocol\n\nMemory Bank artifact type: `\"{N} analysis-items\"` (e.g., `\"45 analysis-items\"`).\n\n**Memory Bank — MANDATORY session-end writes:**\n1. Overwrite `context-pack/active-context.md` with session status, decisions, blockers, key artifacts (see execution-protocol.md Section 4 for schema).\n2. Append one milestone row to `context-pack/progress.md` with artifact count above.\n\n**LAST ACTION — MANDATORY:** Update `_progress.json` status to `COMPLETED` with `completed_at` timestamp.\nIf the session failed, set status to `FAILED` instead.\n\n### Step 6: Emit Harness Outputs Sidecar\n\n**Apply execution-protocol.md Section 11.** Mandatory when the prompt contains a `## Run metadata` block (Stepwise invocation); skip otherwise (standalone invocation). This is the FINAL file write of the run.\n\n**Output parameters this skill produces** (one key per row of the prompt's `## Output parameters` table):\n\n- `analysis_output_path`: the resolved `analysis_output_path` parameter — the SPEC_FOLDER you wrote into.\n\n**Example sidecar contents** (values illustrative):\n\n```json\n{ \"analysis_output_path\": \"/abs/path/to/artifacts/outputs/<capability>/analysis\" }\n```\n\n## Pipeline Position\n\n```\nTest Strategy → Test Cases (from QE Planning)\n                    ↓\n            [analyze-test-cases] ← YOU ARE HERE\n                    ↓\n            [web-discovery]\n                    ↓\n            [automation-planning]\n                    ↓\n            [automation-code-generation]\n                    ↓\n            [code-generation-validation] (manual gate)\n                    ↓\n            [automation-test-execution]\n                    ↓\n            [reporting-analysis]\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nSigns that test case analysis is being conducted superficially:\n\n- Analysis output doesn't reference actual TC IDs from the source file\n- Zero gaps found on a non-trivial test suite (every suite has coverage gaps)\n- All test cases classified as \"automatable\" without justification\n- No complexity distribution (everything marked \"simple\")\n- Summary counts don't match actual items in the analysis\n- Missing traceability to epics/stories when source has mapping\n- Analysis completed without reading test strategy priorities\n- All items marked `status: complete` but no source tags\n\n## Reference File Listing\n\n| File | Purpose | When Loaded |\n|------|---------|-------------|\n| `references/analysis-spec-template.md` | Complete spec structure with example entries | Step 3 start |\n| `references/phase-a-input-validation.md` | Input collection, pre-flight, inventory detection | Phase A |\n| `references/phase-b-quality-analysis.md` | Quality assessment, feasibility, complexity, classification | Phase B |\n| `references/phase-c-document-generation.md` | Spec assembly, gap analysis, open_questions consolidation | Phase C |\n","isError":false}}
