[17:24:47] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9bd5096c781c3b7c","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/_dev/GLB/stepwise-fifa-qa/.coda/skills/analyze-test-cases/references/analysis-spec-template.md\" lines=\"220\" start=\"1\" end=\"220\" returned=\"220\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Analysis Spec Template — ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md\n     2|\n     3|## Template Rules\n     4|\n     5|- **No prose.** Every section is structured data only.\n     6|- **No narrative.** No motivational text, no context paragraphs.\n     7|- **All items carry status:** `complete` | `pending` | `assumption`\n     8|- **All gaps in open_questions.** Single registry, no scatter.\n     9|- **Source tags mandatory.** No source → cannot be `complete`.\n    10|- **ID Format Fidelity:** Use EXACT TC ID format from source. Never renumber.\n    11|- **Technology Neutrality:** Use capability language, not tool-specific names.\n    12|- **Anti-Fade:** Last section must match depth of first section.\n    13|- **Language:** Generate in `{DETECTED_LANGUAGE}`. Default: English.\n    14|\n    15|---\n    16|\n    17|## Spec File Structure\n    18|\n    19|```markdown\n    20|# {project_name} — Test Case Analysis Spec\n    21|version: {version}\n    22|session: {SESSION_ID}\n    23|mode: {BUILD | REPAIR}\n    24|date: {ISO 8601}\n    25|language: {detected_language}\n    26|sources:\n    27|  test_cases: {test_cases_path}\n    28|  test_strategy: {test_strategy_path}\n    29|  test_inventory: {automation_code_path}/test-inventory.md | N/A\n    30|spec_status: {draft | complete}\n    31|```\n    32|\n    33|### Section 1: executive_metrics\n    34|\n    35|```markdown\n    36|## executive_metrics\n    37|\n    38|total_test_cases: {N}\n    39|automatable: {N}\n    40|partial: {N}\n    41|manual_only: {N}\n    42|simple: {N}\n    43|medium: {N}\n    44|complex: {N}\n    45|new: {N}          # 0 if no inventory\n    46|update: {N}       # 0 if no inventory\n    47|duplicate: {N}    # 0 if no inventory\n    48|completeness_score: {avg 1-10}\n    49|gaps_found: {N}\n    50|clarifications_needed: {N}\n    51|status: complete\n    52|```\n    53|\n    54|### Section 2: original_test_cases\n    55|\n    56|```markdown\n    57|## original_test_cases\n    58|\n    59|{VERBATIM content from test_cases_path — no edits, no summaries}\n    60|\n    61|status: complete\n    62|source: {test_cases_path}\n    63|```\n    64|\n    65|### Section 3: quality_assessment\n    66|\n    67|Per-TC structured entries:\n    68|\n    69|```markdown\n    70|## quality_assessment\n    71|\n    72|### {TC_ID}: {title}\n    73|completeness: {score}/10\n    74|validation_points: {defined | missing}\n    75|test_data: {specified | needs_definition}\n    76|edge_cases: {yes | partial | no}\n    77|negative_scenarios: {yes | partial | no}\n    78|feasibility: {automatable | partial | manual_only}\n    79|complexity: {simple | medium | complex}\n    80|justification: {brief reason for feasibility and complexity ratings}\n    81|status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n    82|source: {TC_ID} from {test_cases_path}\n    83|```\n    84|\n    85|Repeat for ALL test cases. Do NOT skip any.\n    86|\n    87|### Section 4: traceability_matrix\n    88|\n    89|```markdown\n    90|## traceability_matrix\n    91|\n    92|| requirement_or_strategy_section | test_cases | coverage | status | source |\n    93||-------------------------------|------------|----------|--------|--------|\n    94|| {strategy section or requirement ID} | TC-XXX, TC-YYY | full | complete | {test_strategy_path} |\n    95|| {uncovered requirement} | — | none | pending | gap analysis |\n    96|```\n    97|\n    98|### Section 5: gap_analysis\n    99|\n   100|```markdown\n   101|## gap_analysis\n   102|\n   103|### GAP-01: {description}\n   104|type: {uncovered_requirement | missing_edge_case | missing_negative_scenario | missing_test_data}\n   105|severity: {high | medium | low}\n   106|affected_tcs: [TC-XXX, TC-YYY]\n   107|recommendation: {suggested action}\n   108|status: complete\n   109|source: traceability analysis\n   110|\n   111|### GAP-02: ...\n   112|```\n   113|\n   114|### Section 6: classification (conditional — only if inventory exists)\n   115|\n   116|```markdown\n   117|## classification\n   118|\n   119|### delta_summary\n   120|new: {count}\n   121|update: {count}\n   122|duplicate: {count}\n   123|\n   124|### TC-XXX\n   125|classification: {new | update | duplicate}\n   126|reason: {why this classification}\n   127|existing_method: {method name from inventory | N/A}\n   128|action: {add | modify | skip}\n   129|changed_fields: [{field1}, {field2}]  # update only\n   130|status: complete\n   131|source: inventory comparison\n   132|```\n   133|\n   134|### Section 7: validations\n   135|\n   136|```markdown\n   137|## validations\n   138|\n   139|| check | result | status |\n   140||-------|--------|--------|\n   141|| V01: tc_coverage | {N}/{total} TCs analyzed | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   142|| V02: classification_completeness | {N}/{total} TCs classified | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   143|| V03: strategy_alignment | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   144|| V04: gap_analysis | {N} gaps identified | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   145|| V05: id_format_fidelity | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   146|| V06: traceability | {N}/{total} mappings preserved | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   147|| V07: source_tags | {N}/{total} items with sources | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   148|| V08: summary_counts | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   149|| V09: anti_fade | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   150|| V10: section_completeness | {N}/{total} sections | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   151|| V11: cross_section_consistency | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   152|| V12: id_uniqueness | {description} | {PASS | FAIL} |\n   153|```\n   154|\n   155|### Section 8: open_questions (ALWAYS LAST)\n   156|\n   157|```markdown\n   158|## open_questions\n   159|\n   160|### pending_inputs\n   161|| id | description | impact_level | source |\n   162||----|-------------|-------------|--------|\n   163|| PI-01 | {what is missing} | {high | medium | low} | {where it was expected} |\n   164|\n   165|### coverage_gaps\n   166|| id | description | affected_area | source |\n   167||----|-------------|---------------|--------|\n   168|| CG-01 | {coverage hole} | {requirement or flow} | {gap analysis} |\n   169|\n   170|### assumptions_to_validate\n   171|| id | assumption | validation_method | risk_if_wrong | source |\n   172||----|-----------|-------------------|---------------|--------|\n   173|| ASM-01 | {what was assumed} | {how to verify} | {impact} | {context} |\n   174|\n   175|### upstream_gaps_carried_forward\n   176|| id | from_artifact | description | local_coverage | source |\n   177||----|---------------|-------------|----------------|--------|\n   178|\n   179|### summary\n   180|total_pending_inputs: {N}\n   181|total_coverage_gaps: {N}\n   182|total_assumptions: {N}\n   183|total_upstream_gaps: {N}\n   184|analysis_status: {PROCEED | CONDITIONAL | BLOCKED}\n   185|```\n   186|\n   187|---\n   188|\n   189|## Generation Rules\n   190|\n   191|### Section Ordering (with dependencies)\n   192|\n   193|1. `executive_metrics` — needs all TC assessments (generate last content, place first)\n   194|2. `original_test_cases` — needs TC_CONTENT only\n   195|3. `quality_assessment` — needs TC_CONTENT + STRATEGY_CONTENT\n   196|4. `traceability_matrix` — needs quality_assessment + STRATEGY_CONTENT\n   197|5. `gap_analysis` — needs traceability_matrix\n   198|6. `classification` — needs inventory (conditional)\n   199|7. `validations` — needs all sections above (runs checks)\n   200|8. `open_questions` — ALWAYS LAST (consolidation pass)\n   201|\n   202|### REPAIR Mode Mechanics\n   203|\n   204|```\n   205|IF OPERATION_MODE == REPAIR:\n   206|  1. Load existing spec\n   207|  2. Match directives to sections/TCs\n   208|  3. Regenerate ONLY targeted content\n   209|  4. Preserve untargeted sections verbatim\n   210|  5. Preserve existing IDs. New items: max(existing) + 1\n   211|  6. ALWAYS rebuild open_questions and validations from scratch\n   212|  7. Increment version\n   213|```\n   214|\n   215|### Scaling Rules\n   216|\n   217|- Expected output: 200-800 lines (single file sufficient)\n   218|- If test suite > 200 TCs: consider manifest + per-TC files pattern\n   219|- Threshold for split: spec exceeds 3,000 lines\n   220|\n</file>","isError":false}}
