ameters — NOT missing data. Per Zero-Invention, no content was fabricated: all TC IDs and strategy\n    24|content below are read verbatim from the real files above. This mismatch is logged as ASM-01 in\n    25|open_questions for pipeline-config correction.\n    26|status: assumption\n    27|source: directory listing of both declared and resolved paths\n    28|\n    29|## executive_metrics\n    30|\n    31|total_test_cases: 367\n    32|automatable: 213\n    33|partial: 152\n    34|manual_only: 2\n    35|simple: 136\n    36|medium: 187\n    37|complex: 44\n    38|new: 367          # no test inventory found — automation_code_path has no test-inventory.md (first run)\n    39|update: 0\n    40|duplicate: 0\n    41|completeness_score: 7.72\n    42|gaps_found: 9\n    43|clarifications_needed: 13\n    44|status: complete\n    45|source: aggregated from quality_assessment section (367/367 TCs) across e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-0{1..7}-e2e-suite.md\n    46|\n    47|## original_test_cases\n    48|\n    49|Source test cases are Gherkin feature files (367 scenarios across 7 epic suites), too large to\n    50|reproduce verbatim in full within this spec without exceeding the 3,000-line split threshold\n    51|(execution-protocol scaling rule; raw source totals 8,769 lines across 7 files). Per Zero-Invention,\n    52|no content was paraphrased or altered — the authoritative verbatim source remains on disk at the\n    53|paths below and is the source-of-record for every TC ID referenced in this spec.\n    54|\n    55|| epic_id | suite_file | tc_count | tc_id_range |\n    56||---------|-----------|----------|-------------|\n    57|| EPIC-001 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-01-e2e-suite.md | 40 | TC_EPIC01_001-040 |\n    58|| EPIC-002 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-02-e2e-suite.md | 45 | TC_EPIC02_001-045 |\n    59|| EPIC-003 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-03-e2e-suite.md | 60 | TC_EPIC03_001-060 |\n    60|| EPIC-004 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-04-e2e-suite.md | 42 | TC_EPIC04_001-042 |\n    61|| EPIC-005 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-05-e2e-suite.md | 48 | TC_EPIC05_001-048 |\n    62|| EPIC-006 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-06-e2e-suite.md | 62 | TC_EPIC06_001-062 |\n    63|| EPIC-007 | e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-07-e2e-suite.md | 70 | TC_EPIC07_001-070 |\n    64|\n    65|status: complete\n    66|source: artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/ (resolved path — see path_resolution_note)\n    67|\n    68|## quality_assessment\n    69|\n    70|Per-TC structured entries (completeness, validation_points, test_data, edge_cases,\n    71|negative_scenarios, feasibility, complexity, justification) were generated for ALL 367/367 test\n    72|cases. Given the volume (367 entries x ~10 lines = ~3,700 lines), the full per-TC detail is\n    73|stored in per-epic sidecar files under `quality-assessment/` (same directory as this spec) per\n    74|the hybrid manifest + per-item file pattern (execution-protocol scaling rule, >200 TC threshold).\n    75|This section holds the per-epic index and aggregate breakdown; every TC below is traceable to its\n    76|full entry in the referenced file.\n    77|\n    78|| epic_id | detail_file | tc_count | automatable | partial | manual_only | simple | medium | complex |\n    79||---------|-------------|----------|-------------|---------|-------------|--------|--------|---------|\n    80|| EPIC-001 | quality-assessment/epic-01-quality-assessment.md | 40 | 34 | 6 | 0 | 16 | 21 | 3 |\n    81|| EPIC-002 | quality-assessment/epic-02-quality-assessment.md | 45 | 26 | 19 | 0 | 26 | 19 | 0 |\n    82|| EPIC-003 | quality-assessment/epic-03-quality-assessment.md | 60 | 47 | 13 | 0 | 32 | 25 | 3 |\n    83|| EPIC-004 | quality-assessment/epic-04-quality-assessment.md | 42 | 35 | 7 | 0 | 14 | 26 | 2 |\n    84|| EPIC-005 | quality-assessment/epic-05-quality-assessment.md | 48 | 23 | 25 | 0 | 16 | 27 | 5 |\n    85|| EPIC-006 | quality-assessment/epic-06-quality-assessment.md | 62 | 21 | 39 | 2 | 23 | 26 | 13 |\n    86|| EPIC-007 | quality-assessment/epic-07-quality-assessment.md | 70 | 27 | 43 | 0 | 9 | 43 | 18 |\n    87|| **TOTAL** | — | **367** | **213** | **152** | **2** | **136** | **187** | **44** |\n    88|\n    89|Each per-epic detail file contains, for every TC_ID in that epic, the full structured entry:\n    90|`completeness`, `validation_points`, `test_data`, `edge_cases`, `negative_scenarios`,\n    91|`feasibility`, `complexity`, `justification`, `status: complete`, and `source` pointing to the\n    92|originating TC ID and suite file. All 367 entries carry `status: complete` with `source` tags\n    93|(V07 source_tags: 367/367 PASS — see validations section).\n    94|\n    95|Notable per-epic drivers behind the feasibility split:\n    96|- EPIC-005 (Multi-language): 25/48 marked `partial` — translated-content correctness requires\n    97|  subjective/visual judgment of Spanish/French text, not just DOM presence.\n    98|- EPIC-006 (Cross-browser expansion): 39/62 marked `partial`, 2 `manual_only` — only Desktop\n    99|  Chrome is validated per test strategy (NFR-004); Firefox/Safari/Edge-specific scenarios need\n   100|  additional browser support, and browser-crash/memory-exhaustion scenarios cannot be reliably\n   101|  automated.\n   102|- EPIC-007 (Responsive design): 43/70 marked `partial` — cross-viewport layout/spacing\n   103|  correctness requires visual judgment beyond DOM assertions.\n   104|\n   105|status: complete\n   106|source: quality-assessment/epic-0{1..7}-quality-assessment.md (367/367 TCs, all status: complete)\n   107|\n   108|## traceability_matrix\n   109|\n   110|| requirement_or_strategy_section | test_cases | coverage | status | source |\n   111||----------------------------------|------------|----------|--------|--------|\n   112|| EPIC-001 Core Navigation Framework (Must Have, FR-001/FR-005) | TC_EPIC01_001-040 | full | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary |\n   113|| EPIC-002 Homepage Validation (Must Have) | TC_EPIC02_001-045 | full | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary |\n   114|| EPIC-003 \"What FIFA Does\" Content Areas (Must Have) | TC_EPIC03_001-060 | full | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary |\n   115|| EPIC-004 Top Navigation Menu Testing (Must Have) | TC_EPIC04_001-042 | full | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary |\n   116|| EPIC-005 Multi-language Framework Support (Should Have) | TC_EPIC05_001-048 | full | assumption | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary (epic status: assumption) |\n   117|| EPIC-006 Cross-browser Expansion (Could Have) | TC_EPIC06_001-062 | full | pending | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary (epic status: pending) |\n   118|| EPIC-007 Responsive Design Testing (Could Have) | TC_EPIC07_001-070 | full | pending | STRATEGY-SPEC scope_summary (epic status: pending) |\n   119|| NFR-001 Page load < 3s | TC_EPIC02 load-time scenarios (partial set) | partial | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC performance_gates |\n   120|| NFR-002 95% test reliability | — | none | pending | STRATEGY-SPEC performance_gates — no dedicated reliability/flakiness TC found |\n   121|| NFR-004 Desktop Chrome browser support | TC_EPIC06_* (Chrome-only subset) | partial | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC performance_gates |\n   122|| QR-005 Page load performance degradation | TC_EPIC02 performance scenarios | partial | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC quality_risks_coverage |\n   123|| QR-009 Website structure changes break tests (robust selectors) | TC_EPIC01_015-022 (Page Object Model) | full | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC quality_risks_coverage |\n   124|| QR-012 Browser compatibility failures | TC_EPIC06_001-062 | full | pending | STRATEGY-SPEC quality_risks_coverage (epic status: pending) |\n   125|| Out of scope: Authentication testing | — | none (by design) | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC out_of_scope |\n   126|| Out of scope: API testing | — | none (by design) | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC out_of_scope |\n   127|| accessibility_strategy: wcag_2.1_aa (P0 pages) | TC_EPIC04_003, TC_EPIC04_026-031 (ARIA/keyboard) | partial | complete | STRATEGY-SPEC cross_cutting |\n   128|| accessibility_strategy: screen_reader (manual, 0% automation) | — | none | pending | STRATEGY-SPEC cross_cutting — no screen-reader TC found; matches strategy's own 0% automation_level |\n   129|\n   130|status: complete\n   131|source: STRATEGY-SPEC-Test-Strategy-1.md scope_summary / quality_risks_coverage / performance_gates / cross_cutting sections, cross-referenced with quality_assessment TC index above\n   132|\n   133|## gap_analysis\n   134|\n   135|### GAP-01: No dedicated test-reliability / flakiness measurement test case\n   136|type: uncovered_requirement\n   137|severity: medium\n   138|affected_tcs: []\n   139|recommendation: Add a TC (or CI-level metric hook) that tracks pass-rate over N runs against the NFR-002 95% reliability target; current suites validate functional behavior only, not suite stability itself.\n   140|status: complete\n   141|source: traceability analysis vs STRATEGY-SPEC performance_gates NFR-002\n   142|\n   143|### GAP-02: No screen-reader validation test case despite accessibility_strategy listing it\n   144|type: missing_negative_scenario\n   145|severity: low\n   146|affected_tcs: []\n   147|recommendation: Strategy already marks screen_reader as `pending` / 0% automation_level (manual_testing) — treat as an accepted manual gap, not an automation defect; flag for the manual test plan instead.\n   148|status: complete\n   149|source: traceability analysis vs STRATEGY-SPEC cross_cutting accessibility_strategy\n   150|\n   151|### GAP-03: EPIC-006 cross-browser scenarios exceed current browser support scope\n   152|type: uncovered_requirement\n   153|severity: medium\n   154|affected_tcs: [TC_EPIC06_* Firefox/Safari/Edge-specific subset (39 TCs flagged partial, 2 manual_only)]\n   155|recommendation: NFR-004 currently scopes validation to Desktop Chrome only; before automating EPIC-006 fully, confirm whether cross-browser infrastructure (Firefox/Safari/Edge runners) will be provisioned, or